kes the offense he ends  this particular fight with a rather  anti-climactic thanos snap but it just  makes the next mob fight the one  starring fujimaru all the more rewarding  [Music]  the altair fight in recreators episode  20 is something similar  this fight compared to the previous one  is similar in a sense that it's part  altair showing off her superiority like  gita as we head towards the climax of  recreators we get a treat in the form of  an episode long fight where it's pretty  much everyone giving their all at altair  and it not even mattering in the end in  spite of the realization that altai has  become the strongest being in the  universe the protagonists do soldier on  and a lot of them go down in a blaze of  glory even the heralded trump card  sirius doesn't get the job done a sirius  only became a vessel for altair to  control this fight was a fight that kept  me on the edge of my seat because i  legit can't think of any way altair  could be defeated after seeing  everything this is yet another example  of a fight that's unwinnable in the  conventional way like ogen was defeated  by ingenuity it would take something  more than direct fighting to put a stop  to altair  [Music]  we de-escalate a bit with princess  connect golem fight  actually de-escalate could be a misnomer  however this may not be a final boss of  any sort like the previous entries but  it doesn't mean that it's any less  intense or epic the golden fight happens  somewhere in the middle of the second  season and this is around the time that  things get real for princess connect  this arc marks the shift in tone where  the serious plot comes in and yuki's  backstory gets revealed and barring a  relatively light-hearted episode or two  the show never lets go of the momentum  it established with this fight this is  pretty much a standard arc finale where  the characters get to show their attacks  as they take on an army of foes flanking  the gigantic boss showing off the  signature mo